[32m+[m[32m| **Login attempt before verification** | Blocked — `AuthService.login()` checks `email_verified` and rejects if FALSE |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Token expires (24 hours)** | Record remains, `verified=FALSE` — user cannot login; new token can be issued via resend |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Token already consumed** | Returns error — single-use enforcement |[m
[32m+[m[32m| **Resend verification** | New `email_verifications` record created, new email sent — old token invalidated by expiry |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Rule:** No user may login until `email_verified = TRUE`. This applies to all user creation paths (invitation acceptance, future self-service).[m
